Most Asked Scenario-Based Questions

# A production server is running very slowly. How would you identify the problematic process?
Answer:

First, I check the system's CPU and memory usage using the top or htop command. These commands show all running processes in real time. I identify the process consuming the highest CPU or memory by checking its PID and process name. Then, I use ps -p <PID> -f to get more details. If the process is stuck or unnecessary, I stop it using the kill command after verifying it is safe to do so.

> Commands
// top
or
// htop
To get details of the process:
// ps -p <PID> -f
To stop the process:
// kill <PID>
If it does not stop:
// kill -9 <PID>


